IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nt-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (nt-seat.l4): a person with a time limit, or who needs to know when something takes effect.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the section named beside it, with the calendar for the weekdays, and not read back from a run.
-- Each question has at least one case that is answered and one that the text does not answer (the value NOTHING), and each yes-or-no limb of a rule has a case on both sides.

§ `Counting my time limit (sections 17 and 28)`

-- The worked periods.
-- Three years from 16 July 2025 ends on Sunday 16 July 2028, so s 28(2) moves it to Monday 17 July 2028.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 "years" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
-- If Monday 17 July 2028 is itself a public holiday, the first day after it that is none of these is Tuesday 18 July 2028.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 "years" TRUE (Date 17 7 2028) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025 ends on Tuesday 15 January 2030: no change.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 "years" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025 ends on Sunday 1 September 2030, so Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 "years" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 ends on Saturday 31 January 2026, so Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Two public holidays in a row after that weekend: Monday 2 and Tuesday 3 February 2026, so Wednesday 4 February 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE (Date 3 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 2 2026)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025 ends on Saturday 28 February 2026, so Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 "months" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024 ends on Thursday 29 February 2024: no change.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 "months" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- One year from 29 February 2024 ends on Friday 28 February 2025: no change.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 "years" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- Twenty-eight days from Monday 3 March 2025 ends on Monday 31 March 2025.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 3 3 2025) 28 "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- One day from Friday 7 March 2025 ends on Saturday 8 March, so Monday 10 March 2025.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 7 3 2025) 1 "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- A holiday that is not on the last day changes nothing; a date given with the answer "no" is ignored.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 "years" TRUE (Date 20 1 2030) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 "years" FALSE (Date 15 1 2030) FALSE (Date 15 1 2030) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- A holiday on a Tuesday last day moves it to Wednesday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 "years" TRUE (Date 15 1 2030) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 1 2030)
-- Not covered: the Act says nothing about weeks, other units, no length, a part of a day, or a negative length.
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 "weeks" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 "fortnights" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 48 "hours" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) 1.5 "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my time limit run out` (Date 1 1 2026) (0 MINUS 3) "days" FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 28(1): the day from which the period runs is left out, so counting starts on the next day.
#ASSERT `Which is the first day counted in my period` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS Date 17 7 2025
#ASSERT `Which is the first day counted in my period` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `Which is the first day counted in my period` (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `Which is the first day counted in my period` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 1 3 2024

-- ss 28(1), 28(1A): a period running "from" the day leaves it out; a period ending "at", "with" or "on" it counts it.
#ASSERT `Does the day of the event itself count as one of my days` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the day of the event itself count as one of my days` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 28(2): Saturday 31 January 2026, Sunday 1 February 2026 and a public holiday are rest days; Monday 2 February 2026 is not, unless it is a holiday.
#ASSERT `Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT `Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT `Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT `Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE (Date 3 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday where I must act` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 2 2 2026)))

-- s 28(2): the first day on or after the last day that is not a rest day.
#ASSERT `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
#ASSERT `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
#ASSERT `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE (Date 3 2 2026) EQUALS Date 4 2 2026
#ASSERT `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` (Date 3 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
#ASSERT `If my last day is a rest day, on which day may I act` (Date 16 7 2028) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 17 7 2028

-- s 17 "business day": not a Saturday, not a Sunday, not a public holiday.
#ASSERT `Is this day a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a business day` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a business day` (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this day a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT `Is this day a business day` (Date 3 2 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)

-- s 17 "calendar month": a month beginning at the start of 15 January 2025 ends at the end of 14 February 2025;
-- one beginning on 1 January 2025 ends on 31 January 2025; one beginning on 31 January 2024 ends on 29 February 2024; one beginning on 31 December 2025 ends on 30 January 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS Date 14 2 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 31 1 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `On which day does a calendar month that starts on this day end` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 30 1 2026

-- s 17 "calendar year" runs from 1 January to 31 December; s 17 "financial year" runs from 1 July to 30 June.
#ASSERT `On which day does the calendar year end` 2025 EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does the calendar year end` 2024 EQUALS Date 31 12 2024
#ASSERT `On which day does the financial year start` 2026 EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does the financial year start` 2025 EQUALS Date 1 7 2024

§ `My age (sections 17 and 30)`

-- s 30: the anniversary of a birth on 15 June 2000 in 2018 is 15 June 2018; a birth on 29 February 2008 has its anniversary on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day do I reach a given age` (Date 15 6 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2018)
#ASSERT `On which day do I reach a given age` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Not covered: an age of nought years.
#ASSERT `On which day do I reach a given age` (Date 15 6 2000) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 17 "adult": an individual who has attained the age of 18 years.
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` TRUE (Date 16 7 2007) (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` TRUE (Date 16 7 2007) (Date 15 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` TRUE (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` TRUE (Date 29 2 2008) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` FALSE (Date 16 7 2007) (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 17 "infant": a person who has not attained the age of 18 years.
#ASSERT `Am I an infant on a given day` (Date 16 7 2007) (Date 15 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an infant on a given day` (Date 16 7 2007) (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Times of day (section 29)`

#ASSERT `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` 0 9 0 5 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 9, `minutes after the hour` IS 5)
#ASSERT `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` 2 3 5 9 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 23, `minutes after the hour` IS 59)
#ASSERT `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 0, `minutes after the hour` IS 0)
-- Not covered: 1260 has no 60th minute and 2400 is not a time on the day.
#ASSERT `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` 1 2 6 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What time after midnight does a time written as four digits mean` 2 4 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `When something takes effect (sections 5, 6, 6A and 63B)`

-- s 5: a particular day.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "on a particular day" (Date 1 7 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2023)
-- s 5: a day fixed by Gazette notice, once fixed; before it is fixed the day is not covered.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice" (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 10 8 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 8 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5: the happening of an event, once it has happened.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "on the happening of an event" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2024)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "on the happening of an event" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5: no commencement stated, so the day after assent is declared (28 February 2024 is in a leap year).
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
-- Not covered: some other way of stating it.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act or a provision of an Act commence` "tomorrow" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 6: not before the Gazette notification of the Governor-General's assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General first have effect` (Date 1 7 2023) TRUE (Date 15 7 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General first have effect` (Date 1 7 2023) TRUE (Date 20 6 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General first have effect` (Date 1 7 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 6A: the start of the day, unless the Act provides a time of day.
#ASSERT `At what time of that day does an Act or a provision commence` (Date 1 7 2023) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 1 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 0, `minutes after the hour` IS 0)
#ASSERT `At what time of that day does an Act or a provision commence` (Date 1 7 2023) TRUE 14 30 EQUALS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 1 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 14, `minutes after the hour` IS 30)

-- s 63B(1), (2): the day specified, or the day of an event.
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "on a particular day" (Date 1 8 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "on the happening of an event" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 9 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "on the happening of an event" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: subsection (2) does not mention a day fixed by Gazette notice.
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "on a day to be fixed by Gazette notice" (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 8 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 63B(5): silent, so the day after it is made (a regulation, or a rule or by-law that is on the website).
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 28 2 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2023)
-- s 63B(6): silent, and a rule or by-law not published or to be published on the website, so the day it is notified in the Gazette.
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day does a regulation, rule or by-law commence` "it does not say" (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 63B(3), (4): a start before the day it is made, with no express provision in the Act, is of no effect.
#ASSERT `Is a provision starting before the day it was made of no effect` (Date 9 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a provision starting before the day it was made of no effect` (Date 9 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is a provision starting before the day it was made of no effect` (Date 10 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is a provision starting before the day it was made of no effect` (Date 11 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `When a document is taken to be served (section 25)`

-- s 25(2): prepaid post, when it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by prepaid post" (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE (Date 14 3 2023) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by prepaid post" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 25(3): fax, when it was sent to a current fax number, subject to evidence to the contrary.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by fax" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2023)
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by fax" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by fax" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 25(4): left at the address, when it was left with the person.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by leaving it at the address" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2023)
-- Not covered: subsections (2) to (4) do not speak of a document given to a person, nor of any other way.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by giving it to a person" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is a document taken to be served` "by email" (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 25(1): who may be served in what way.
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by giving it to someone" "the recipient" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` TRUE "by giving it to someone" "the recipient" FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` TRUE "by giving it to someone" "an executive officer of the body" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by giving it to someone" "an executive officer of the body" FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by giving it to someone" "a person authorised by the recipient" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` TRUE "by giving it to someone" "a person authorised by the recipient" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` TRUE "by giving it to someone" "someone else" FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by prepaid post" "none" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` TRUE "by fax" "none" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by leaving it at the address" "none" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by leaving it at the address" "none" FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by leaving it at the address" "none" TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I serve my document in this way` FALSE "by email" "none" TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sitting days of the Legislative Assembly (sections 63, 63C and 64)`

-- A calendar of twenty sitting days of the Legislative Assembly in 2025, numbered here by their order:
-- 1: 4 Mar, 2: 5 Mar, 3: 6 Mar, 4: 25 Mar, 5: 26 Mar, 6: 27 Mar, 7: 8 Apr, 8: 9 Apr, 9: 10 Apr, 10: 29 Apr,
-- 11: 30 Apr, 12: 1 May, 13: 13 May, 14: 14 May, 15: 15 May, 16: 3 Jun, 17: 4 Jun, 18: 5 Jun, 19: 17 Jun, 20: 18 Jun.
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`a calendar of sitting days in 2025` MEANS
    LIST Date 4 3 2025, Date 5 3 2025, Date 6 3 2025, Date 25 3 2025, Date 26 3 2025, Date 27 3 2025, Date 8 4 2025, Date 9 4 2025, Date 10 4 2025, Date 29 4 2025,
         Date 30 4 2025, Date 1 5 2025, Date 13 5 2025, Date 14 5 2025, Date 15 5 2025, Date 3 6 2025, Date 4 6 2025, Date 5 6 2025, Date 17 6 2025, Date 18 6 2025

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`a calendar of three sitting days` MEANS LIST Date 4 3 2025, Date 5 3 2025, Date 6 3 2025

-- s 63(b): made on Monday 3 March 2025, before the first sitting day, the 6th sitting day after is no. 6, 27 March.
#ASSERT `By which day must a regulation be tabled` (Date 3 3 2025) `a calendar of sitting days in 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 27 3 2025)
-- Made on a sitting day, 4 March: that day is left out (s 28(1)), so the 6th sitting day after is no. 7, 8 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must a regulation be tabled` (Date 4 3 2025) `a calendar of sitting days in 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 8 4 2025)
-- Not covered: the calendar names too few sitting days.
#ASSERT `By which day must a regulation be tabled` (Date 3 3 2025) `a calendar of three sitting days` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 63A(2)(b): notified in the Gazette on 25 March 2025 (a sitting day), the 6th after is no. 10, 29 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must a rule or by-law be tabled` (Date 25 3 2025) `a calendar of sitting days in 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By which day must a rule or by-law be tabled` (Date 25 3 2025) `a calendar of three sitting days` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 63C(3): tabled as required on 27 March 2025, the 12th sitting day after is no. 18, 5 June.
#ASSERT `By which day must notice of a resolution to disallow subordinate legislation be given` TRUE (Date 27 3 2025) (Date 25 3 2025) `a calendar of sitting days in 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 6 2025)
-- Not tabled as required, the 12th sitting day after the last day it was required to be tabled (25 March) is no. 16, 3 June.
#ASSERT `By which day must notice of a resolution to disallow subordinate legislation be given` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 25 3 2025) `a calendar of sitting days in 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 3 6 2025)
#ASSERT `By which day must notice of a resolution to disallow subordinate legislation be given` TRUE (Date 27 3 2025) (Date 25 3 2025) `a calendar of three sitting days` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 64(2): disallowed on 15 March 2025, the 6 months end on 15 September 2025.
#ASSERT `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 15 9 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 9 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: legislation that is not the same in substance, and has not the same effect, is not dealt with in subsection (2).
#ASSERT `May subordinate legislation like disallowed legislation be made on this day` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `If a law I relied on has been repealed or has expired (sections 11 to 16)`

-- s 12(c): the repeal does not affect a right or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired or incurred under it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired or incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(d): the same for a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against the repealed Act.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act wipe out a penalty I incurred under it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act wipe out a penalty I incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12: a legal proceeding about such a right may be instituted, continued or enforced as if the repealing Act had not been made.
#ASSERT `May a proceeding about a right or liability under a repealed Act still be started or continued` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a proceeding about a right or liability under a repealed Act still be started or continued` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 14: the repealed provisions continue in force until the substituted provisions commence.
#ASSERT `Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2023) (Date 30 6 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2023) (Date 1 7 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2023) (Date 2 7 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do the repealed provisions still apply on this day` FALSE (Date 1 7 2023) (Date 30 6 2023) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 15: a reference to the provision repealed is taken to be a reference to the provision re-enacted.
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "an Act" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "a Commonwealth Act or legislative instrument" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "a State, Territory or New Zealand Act or subordinate legislation" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "an Act" FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "an Act" TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: some other kind of law.
#ASSERT `Does a reference to a repealed provision now mean the provision that replaced it` "a treaty" TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Fines and penalties (sections 38DC, 38F and 38G)`

-- s 38DC(3): 5 times the maximum for an individual when the Act authorises the maximum and gives no different one for a body corporate.
#ASSERT `What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation` TRUE FALSE 20 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation` TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most a company may be fined under subordinate legislation` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38F(2): not more than 100 penalty units, subject to the Act under which the legislation is made.
#ASSERT `Is the fine in this subordinate legislation within the limit` 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the fine in this subordinate legislation within the limit` 101 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the fine in this subordinate legislation within the limit` 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38G: a civil penalty not exceeding the penalty specified or prescribed.
#ASSERT `Is the civil penalty I am asked to pay within what the provision allows` 200 200 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the civil penalty I am asked to pay within what the provision allows` 200 199 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the civil penalty I am asked to pay within what the provision allows` 200 201 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Forms, appeals, money due and reprints (sections 65B, 68, 69 and 72B)`

-- s 68: substantial compliance, or as much as the circumstances allow, is sufficient; the section does not say that less is insufficient.
#ASSERT `Is my compliance with a prescribed form good enough` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my compliance with a prescribed form good enough` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my compliance with a prescribed form good enough` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 65B(1): subordinate legislation may provide for review or appeal of a decision made under it or under its Act.
#ASSERT `Can subordinate legislation give me a right of appeal or review` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can subordinate legislation give me a right of appeal or review` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 69: recoverable in a court or tribunal with civil jurisdiction in the Territory to the extent of the amount due.
#ASSERT `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` TRUE 5000 TRUE 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` TRUE 5000 TRUE 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` TRUE 5000 TRUE 4000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` TRUE 5000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money due under an Act be recovered in this court or tribunal` FALSE 5000 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72B: an amendment that commences after the date stated in the reprint is left out unless marked uncommenced.
#ASSERT `Does the reprint I am reading include this amendment` (Date 21 4 2023) (Date 21 4 2023) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the reprint I am reading include this amendment` (Date 22 4 2023) (Date 21 4 2023) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the reprint I am reading include this amendment` (Date 22 4 2023) (Date 21 4 2023) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
